{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Jacob sent messengers before him.</b> Rashi explained: actual angels. Some say he inferred this from the juxtaposition of this sending to the verse ״וַיִּפְגְּעוּ בוֹ מַלְאֲכֵי אֱלֹהִים״ (Genesis 32:2). And some say it is an acrostic of the initial letters of מַחֲנַיִם — from that host Jacob took angels. And Rabbeinu Behaye explained that he inferred it from the fact that it is written ״וַיָּשֻׁבוּ הַמַּלְאָכִים״, and we find no mention that they went, because before they had gone they already returned. And one may explain further that he inferred it from the expression ״לְפָנָיו״, which is mentioned only here — for behold it is written (Numbers 20:14) ״וַיִּשְׁלַח מֹשֶׁה מַלְאָכִים״, and it is written (Numbers 21:21) ״וַיִּשְׁלַח יִשְׂרָאֵל מַלְאָכִים״, and ״לְפָנָיו״ is not mentioned. Rather, this is because here Scripture speaks of actual angels, whose way is to go before him, as it is written (Exodus 23:23) ״כִּי יֵלֵךְ מַלְאָכִי לְפָנֶיךָ״. And he hinted that they were before him always, even at the time they were with Esau, and they were seen in two places far distant from one another — and this is impossible except with actual angels. And if you wish to explain ״וַיָּשֻׁבוּ הַמַּלְאָכִים״ in the sense of the return of words, that they answered him concerning his matters, ״בָּאנוּ אֶל אָחִיךָ״ — then it will be proven from within it that they were actual angels."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:25.161616854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}